---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const desc = 'Free AI calculators: token cost, GPU VRAM, context window fit, training cost, energy and carbon, and AI ROI. No signup, nothing uploaded, answers instantly.';
const jsonld = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'CollectionPage',
  name: 'AI Calculators',
  description: desc,
  url: 'https://theworldofai.org/calculators/',
});
---
<Base title="AI Calculators: cost, memory, context, energy, and ROI — The World of AI" description={desc} current="/calculators/" jsonld={jsonld}>
  <p class="meta-line"><a href="/ai-ecosystem/">AI Ecosystem</a> ·
    <a href="/ai-ecosystem/enterprise-applications-governance-and-tools/">Enterprise Applications, Governance and Tools</a></p>
  <h1>AI Calculators</h1>
  <p class="answer">Six working tools for the questions that decide whether an AI project is
    viable: <b>what it costs to run</b>, <b>what hardware it needs</b>, <b>whether your input
    fits</b>, <b>what a training run costs</b>, <b>what it burns</b>, and <b>whether it pays
    back</b>. Everything runs in your browser. Nothing you type is uploaded or stored.</p>

  <h2>Cost and return</h2>
  <ul class="grid">
    <li class="card">
      <a href="/calculators/token-cost/">LLM Token Cost Calculator</a>
      <p>Turn per-million-token pricing and your usage into a monthly bill.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="card">
      <a href="/calculators/training-cost/">Training Cost Estimator</a>
      <p>GPU hours and dollars for a pre-training or fine-tuning run, from parameters and tokens.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="card">
      <a href="/calculators/roi/">AI ROI Calculator</a>
      <p>Payback period and the adoption rate a deployment has to hit to break even.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Capacity and footprint</h2>
  <ul class="grid">
    <li class="card">
      <a href="/calculators/vram/">GPU VRAM Estimator</a>
      <p>How much memory a model needs at FP16, 8-bit, or 4-bit, with headroom for context.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="card">
      <a href="/calculators/context-window/">Context Window Calculator</a>
      <p>Words, pages, or characters into tokens, and whether it fits with room for the answer.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="card">
      <a href="/calculators/energy-carbon/">Energy and Carbon Estimator</a>
      <p>Kilowatt hours and CO2e from GPU hours, datacenter PUE, and grid intensity.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="meta-line">Each tool shows its own arithmetic and says what it leaves out, so you can
    check the answer rather than trust it. These are planning tools, not financial or legal
    advice: see our <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>.</p>
</Base>
